.he "mkdir (1)                    8/12/26                    mkdir (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
mkdir
- make directories
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
mkdir [ -pvn ] dirname ...
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Mkdir makes each named directory.
.sp
Micronix has no mkdir system call.  The directory is made the way v7
made it: the entry is created, and the two entries every directory
must have - "." pointing at itself and ".." at its parent - are linked
in afterwards.  A directory that exists but has no "." in it was
interrupted between those steps.
.sp
The parent directory must be writable.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-p	Make any missing parent directories too, and do not complain if the directory already exists.

.ti -10
-v	Name each directory as it is made.

.ti -10
-n	Go through the motions without making anything.

.ti -10
-h	Print the usage line.

.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
